.TH "PB-RECORDINGS-KEY-RESET" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-recordings-key-reset - Replace a recording key nobody holds any more; older recordings become unreadable


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb recordings key reset [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Reset the team's recording key when nobody holds it any more.

.PP
Only the team owner can. The new key is made here and signed with your ENV vault's writer key, the identity the ENV team-vault reset uses; machines accept it only because that signature verifies under the key they pinned for the team, never because the server says so. Everyone who can replay gets a copy of the new key. Recordings made before cannot be opened by anyone, you included: use \fBpb recordings key replace\fR instead while any member still holds the key.

.PP
Needs an unlocked ENV vault (\fBpb env unlock\fR).

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--confirm\fP=""
	the team id, typed to confirm

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for reset

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--team\fP=""
	team whose key to reset; defaults to the active workspace


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-recordings-key(1)\fP
